92186410419 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410419 #edb/ref 1069 "q-138856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410419 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410419 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}.$ Its derivative is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410419 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29625a08-0232-5ce8-97e1-f2bb9cf1a9d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410419 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =5x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(5x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))+(5x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =5\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+5x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-5x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{5x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1045 "Logarithmic Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186413631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413607 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8ddfa349-33f9-52db-ae99-fde6c1886942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413608 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413608 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413608 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07b2dd31-87ef-57c3-a041-f20e700d80c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413609 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413609 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413609 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13f20f22-f41f-5f1b-8d9d-f2adb8019550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413610 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413610 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413610 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21ede1b3-ec6b-56c3-a5bd-57ae68918058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413611 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x" #